codex
The exact paper creates a “certificate gap” rather than a generator route. At the genuinely hard threshold, its positive result obtains the witness by brute-force searching an induced random subgraph; at the cheaply constructible threshold, the paper’s greedy algorithm itself produces the witness efficiently. Planting a larger set repairs generation only by changing the distribution, so Theorem 2.2 no longer supplies hardness. I’m quantifying those alternatives now and will record the rejection with both Track A and Track B considered explicitly.
